conference:
  name: "The 3rd International Conference on Advances in Machine Intelligence and Cybersecurity Technologies (AMICT 2026)"
  location: "Labuan, Malaysia"
  start: 2026-11-12
  end: 2026-11-13
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  Equirectangular 360-degree video is stored at 4K-8K for the full sphere even
  though a viewer sees only a viewport, so content-aware retargeting can shrink
  that raster before any viewport is extracted. On crowd panoramas, cyclic
  routing, spherical energy, and semantic protection help only in specific
  regimes: a cyclic spherical baseline already misses most compact heads, and
  always-on person protection is therefore wasted on most scenes. We propose
  content-conditioned cyclic seam carving, which applies cyclic routing and
  spherical energy on every image and adds semantic energy only when a
  SegFormer-B0 estimate of baseline person-hit risk is high. On PanoCount
  medium-density val+test (171 images) the gate fires on 56 images and lowers a
  ground-truth body-hit proxy from 12.59% to 11.04% (-1.55 pp, 95% CI
  [-2.75, -0.35]); on that subset the change is -4.73 pp (17/56 increase).
  An oracle that sees ground-truth columns reaches -35.2 pp on a high-risk
  subset, and always-on predicted-person energy lowers instance hit from 18.68%
  to 5.16%. Sparse temporal sampling can fabricate unsupported apparent yaw.
keywords:
  - equirectangular panorama
  - seam carving
  - 360-degree video
  - viewport
  - semantic protection
  - cyclic routing
  - content-aware retargeting
  - crowd panoramas
